- Copy link and Copy as Markdown have no home: they were to be title-menu actions, and the title chip is gone while crumb menus carry no actions. They belong in the editor's own menu or toolbar, shared by the dock and Editor tabs. No document-level implementation exists; decide first what a copied link is (the canonical Context URI such as `scratch://@arc-one/beats.md`, or an app URL) and how Markdown is read from the live session. All three are owner decisions ([KB: dock document](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow-docs/blob/main/kb/decisions/writer-ux/interaction/documents/dock-document.md)).
- `../context/viewers/ReadOnlyViewerFrame.tsx`: it paints `bg-background`, which a binary file shown in the dock draws against the dock's material. Make it transparent when the host is the dock. No Scratch file reaches it today.
- `DockDocumentView.tsx` and `features/editor/SyncStatus.tsx`: confirm the writer can see "Saved locally (offline)" in the dock. The PR 1 probe found the label in the DOM, but the screenshot showed only the app-wide `ConnectionBanner` ("Reconnecting…"). It also saw the offline label linger in a hidden warm Editor tab after reconnect until reload. Neither was reproduced as a visible bug. Evidence: `work/thread-ux/sidebar-editor/probe.md` in the docs repo.
- `../mobile/MobileDocumentHost.tsx`: a full-screen lineage note has no title pill (mock P3) to reach the chat's Scratch again; the writer opens the menu drawer, whose Scratch section lists it. Decide whether the pill is worth building once Copy link and Copy as Markdown are decided.
